    <statement><p>Suppose <m>Q = 30.8(0.751)^t</m>.
Give the starting value <m>a</m>, the growth
<em>factor</em> <m>b</m>, and the
growth <em>rate</em> <m>r</m> if
<m>Q = a \cdot b^t = a(1+r)^t</m>.</p>
<p><m>a =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>b =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>r =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> %</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>30.8</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.751</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-24.9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



We have <m>a = 30.8</m>, <m>b = 0.751</m>, and
<m>r = b - 1 = 0.751 - 1 = -0.249 = -24.9</m>%.



</solution>
